      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-21T17:18:50Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): wire-iso writes each dimension word with a decimal point\n\nMany wire controls read a number without a decimal point in their\nleast input unit (0.001 mm), so X5 moved 5 um there, not 5 mm. The\nwire-iso post now writes every X, Y, U, V, I, J and taper angle word\nwith its point (X5., Y0., U0., A3.), as the Sodick post already does.\nComment text keeps its plain numbers. The eight wire-iso goldens move\nby the point only; wire_iso_decimal pins the rule over each golden.\n\nFixes #3206\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
